    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d973">

                <pb facs="0899" n="809" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav02/pg809"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 860d.00/258</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Russia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Francis</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-09-05T16:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">September 5,
                                1918, 4 p.m.</hi></date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>247. Your 362, August 13, 6 p.m. This Government has hitherto refrained from any
                    expression of opinion or policy as to the independence of Finland. It therefore
                    deems publication of your statement-inadvisable at present and the Legation at
                    Stockholm has been so informed, adding that as the publication of any appeal
                    from the Finns through us might be construed as intervention in Finnish internal
                    affairs, its publication in that manner at this time appears equally
                    inadvisable.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Lansing</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
